docs/writing-instruments.md:61:## Why Sentence Lab feels broken (verified in code)
docs/writing-instruments.md:63:1. **The "earlier tries" are mid-edit snapshots, not attempts.** `struggle-tracker.ts:85` commits a version after every 1.2 s pause, and `commitVersion` (`struggle-signals.ts`) stores the previous wording whenever exactly one sentence changed. A pause in the middle of a word records something like `The river carr the town's memory.` as an attempt.
docs/writing-instruments.md:88:- **They don't fix the foundation.** Positional identity, polluted attempts, fragile 14-word regex anchors, and the Convex-client gate in front of the writer's own judgement endpoint (`struggle-tracker.ts` `ask`: `if (!client) throw new Error("offline")`) would also undermine every new card.
docs/writing-instruments.md:116:## Instrument 1: the Sentence bench (replaces Sentence Lab)
docs/writing-instruments.md:131:The bench opens from a struggle signal (three _settled_ rewrites), after a sentence has moved twice (opens on Place), or on request from the selection menu or a shortcut.
docs/writing-instruments.md:307:2. Let callers use a custom judgement endpoint without a Convex client (audit gap 8; also `struggle-tracker.ts` `ask`).
